[content]
<div class="container-fluid">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-lg-12">
            <h1>PbClasses - The framework for web-based projects</h1>
            <h4>for businesses, freelancers, and private projects</h4>
        </div>        
    </div>


    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
            <h2>For Businesses</h2>
            <p>The backend system runs on MySQL or MariaDB and is ideally suited for rapidly developing database-driven applications.</p>
            <p>A system for displaying and editing tables using customizable input tools opens up a wide range of potential applications.</p>
            <p>A task system enables the management of scheduled applications running in the background.</p>

            <p><a class="btn btn-default" href="/demos/table-demo.php" role="button" target="_blank">Table Demo &raquo;</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
            <h2>For Freelancers</h2>
            <p>Many freelancers want to automate—or at least simplify—routine tasks.</p>
            <p>This system allows for the rapid programming of custom office solutions.</p>
            <p>It utilizes external libraries such as TCPDF for PDF generation and JsTree for displaying and manipulating tree structures.
                Combined, these can be used to program tools like quote configurators or other document-creation aids.</p>

        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
            <h2>For Agencies</h2>
            <p>This system enables web agencies—even those without deep programming expertise—to offer their clients
                custom solutions that go beyond the scope of standard WordPress plugins.</p>
            <p><b>PbClasses</b> can be adapted for a wide variety of use cases and, thanks to AJAX support, easily integrated into existing projects.</p>
            <p>Another advantage: The system's templates are interchangeable and fully editable. You can therefore present your customers with a solution of your own.</p>

        </div>
    </div> 
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
            <h2>Objective</h2>
            <p>Why another PHP framework? - <b>PbClasses</b> is a system that seeks to bring back some of PHP's original simplicity
                by focusing on specific requirements and target audiences while omitting unnecessary features. 
                
                PbClasses is primarily intended as a codebase for backend systems, application platforms, and intranet solutions that can be rapidly developed using it.

However, it can also operate on a small scale, running in the background or complementing existing systems.
            </p>

        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
            <h2>Technical Background</h2>
<p>Predecessors of this system have been successfully in use for more than 15 years. 
                The current version runs on PHP 8 and implements the PSR-4 standard. </p>
            <p>PbClasses and its underlying base system evolved organically over the course of many projects spanning more than 15 years.
            It is a system born of practical experience with recurring tasks, rather than theoretical considerations at the drawing board. </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
            <h2>Project Examples</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Admin panels for web projects</li>
                <li>Local systems for home offices</li>
                <li>Management of business processes</li>
                <li>Intranets</li>
                <li>Extensions for existing projects</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p><i>The text was translated from German by Google Translate.</i></p>
</div>



